    "durationMs": 199375,
    "finalText": "Done. The URL Shortener API is complete and verified end-to-end.\n\n**What I built:**\n- `database/migrations/2026_11_22_000000_create_links_table.php` — `links` table (unique `code`, `text` `url`, `clicks` counter)\n- `app/Models/Link.php` — Eloquent model with integer click cast\n- `app/Http/Controllers/LinkController.php` — create (201/409/422), show (200/404), redirect (302 + atomic single click increment), list (`items`+`total`, ascending by id)\n- `routes/api.php` + `bootstrap/app.php` with `apiPrefix: ''` so paths are `/links`, `/links/{code}`, `/r/{code}` with no `/api` prefix — plus mirrored `/projects/*` routes since the spec was ambiguous about that base path\n- `start.sh` (executable) — `php artisan migrate --force` then `php artisan serve --host=0.0.0.0 --port=8000 --no-reload` in the foreground; README has a \"Running the URL Shortener API\" section\n\n**Verified by curl against the running server:** 201 with exact submitted URLs (slashes/`&`/fragments unescaped), generated 8-char codes, 409 on duplicate custom codes, 422 for malformed JSON / junk / `ftp:` / hostless URLs / bad codes, 302 with byte-exact `Location`, clicks incrementing exactly once, correct list shape and order, and all data surviving a full server restart. DB credentials come solely from the `DB_*` environment variables, test data was truncated, and my server is stopped so port 8000 is free for the harness."
